        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>AROER</strong> ruins. (1.) A town on the north bank of the Arnon (Deuteronomy 4:48; Judges 11:26; 2 Kings 10:33), the southern boundary of the kingdom of Sihon (Joshua 12:2). It is now called Arair, 13 miles west of the Dead Sea. (2.) One of the towns built by the tribe of Gad (Numbers 32:34) “before Rabbah” (Joshua 13:25), the Ammonite capital. It was famous in the history of Jephthah (Judges 11:33) and of David (2 Samuel 24:5). (Comp. Isaiah 17:2; 2 Kings 15:29.) (3.) A city in the south… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
