    (
        8,
        3,
        "",
        "man does not live by bread only",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The wilderness pedagogy.</strong> Manna as theological lesson: the dependence of the body on God’s sustained word, not merely on natural processes. Jesus quotes this verse to the tempter in the wilderness (Matt 4:4, Luke 4:4). The deeper context in Deut 8 is a meditation on prosperity’s spiritual danger — the warning that when the people enter a land of plenty, they will be tempted to forget the lean years that taught them dependence.",
        "User original",
    ),
