        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>FOUNTAIN</strong> (Hebrews ‘ain; i.e., “eye” of the water desert), a natural source of living water. Palestine was a “land of brooks of water, of fountains, and depths that spring out of valleys and hills” (Deuteronomy 8:7; 11:11). These fountains, bright sparkling “eyes” of the desert, are remarkable for their abundance and their beauty, especially on the west of Jordan. All the perennial rivers and streams of the country are supplied from fountains, and depend comparatively little on… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
