    (
        18,
        15,
        "",
        "a  prophet from among you",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The prophet like Moses.</strong> A foundational messianic text in Second Temple Judaism. Read variously as Joshua, the prophetic line as a whole, or a specific eschatological figure. Acts 3:22 and 7:37 apply it to Jesus; the Samaritan tradition applies it to the <em>Taheb</em>; the Qumran community to a coming prophet alongside two messiahs. The verse marks Israel’s transition from direct theophany at Sinai (which the people couldn’t bear, 18:16) to mediated prophecy — and the long expectation of one prophet who would speak with Mosaic immediacy again.",
        "User original",
    ),
