    (
        27,
        15,
        "",
        "Cursed is the man who makes",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The covenant ceremony at Ebal and Gerizim.</strong> Six tribes on Mount Gerizim recite blessings, six on Mount Ebal recite curses; the Levites speak the formal liturgy in the valley between. Twelve curses, each answered by a public “Amen.” The setting is geographically dramatic — Gerizim and Ebal still stand in the West Bank as facing peaks above modern Nablus. The Samaritan community (whose temple stood on Gerizim) reads the order of mountains differently, with Gerizim as the mountain of blessing and the primary cult site — a textual variant traceable back to manuscripts like the Samaritan Pentateuch.",
        "User original",
    ),
