        "dict-easton",
        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>EAGLE</strong> (Herb. nesher; properly the griffon vulture or great vulture, so called from its tearing its prey with its beak), referred to for its swiftness of flight (Deuteronomy 28:49; 2 Samuel 1:23), its mounting high in the air (Job 39:27), its strength (Psalm 103:5), its setting its nest in high places (Jeremiah 49:16), and its power of vision (Job 39:27-30). This “ravenous bird” is a symbol of those nations whom God employs and sends forth to do a work of destruction, sweeping away… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
